{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgT9chVR2ZeTZevbsfnse","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PWp3QsYE7KZVMmzvfrocH2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nS=lambda *a:list(a)\nd={\n\"status\":\"ready\",\n\"selected_prompt_family\":\"paper_standalone\",\n\"recommended_title\":\"How Far Can Five Cheap Graph Statistics Go? Log-Linear Cover-Time Prediction on Small Connected Graphs\",\n\"central_question\":\"For connected graphs with 6<=n<=30, does a ridge model on a handful of cheap graph statistics (n, m, mean degree, max degree, diameter) predict Monte Carlo start-averaged random-walk cover time with lower family-macro log error than the generic 2m(n-1) bound?\",\n\"central_thesis\":\"On the sealed held-out graphs, a five-statistic log-linear ridge predictor (family-macro log MAE 0.181) is far closer to Monte Carlo cover times than the 2m(n-1) bound (1.754) and than constant and label-shuffled controls (0.870, 1.423), with median Monte Carlo relative SE about 0.029; this is measured only on 12 synthetic families, 24 test graphs, and the question of which families it fails on is not answered by the retained evidence.\",\n\"narrative_rationale\":\"The only grounded, completed evidence is the sealed final evaluation (outcome qualified, status completed) of the frozen selection, which is the seed baseline ridge predictor (study.selection_kind=baseline; investigation completed_no_winner; 1 attempt, 0 scored, 1 unscored; search score delta 0.0). The strongest honest story is therefore a calibrated, narrow empirical-measurement paper: a cheap-statistic log-linear predictor versus the worst-case bound and sanity controls, with explicit scope limits. No improvement over a baseline is claimed because the studied method IS the baseline; the unscored resistance/Matthews variant has no performance evidence and is not a result. The second half of the research question (error vs graph type) cannot be answered quantitatively because per-family metrics are absent from paper_data; the paper must say so (unknown, not a failure) and use the family design only as a description of the test distribution and as a stated limitation/future-work item.\",\n\"prior_paper_story_status\":\"preserved\",\n\"edit_framing_decision\":\"Not edit mode: no previous_paper or staged inputs exist (edit-context placeholders are unfilled), so there is no prior story to preserve or replace; field value is nominal. Fresh thesis-first framing chosen over a Matthews/resistance-predictor story, which lacks any scored evidence.\",\n\"staged_input_impact\":[\"No staged paper, program, or result inputs were provided; framing is based solely on paper_data.json final_evaluation and downstream_study.\"],\n\"method_groups\":[\n{\"name\":\"Five-statistic log-linear ridge predictor (frozen selection)\",\"role\":\"proposed\",\"include_reason\":\"This is the studied method (frozen selection = seed baseline program): standardized log n, log m, log mean degree, log max degree, log diameter; ridge (lambda=1, unpenalised intercept) on log cover time, fit in-episode on labelled training graphs; exact method visible in source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py.\"},\n{\"name\":\"Generic 2m(n-1) worst-case bound\",\"role\":\"baseline\",\"include_reason\":\"The comparator named in the research question (Aleliunas et al.); final bound macro log MAE 1.754. Also the fallback when no training data is supplied.\"},\n{\"name\":\"Constant predictor control\",\"role\":\"baseline\",\"include_reason\":\"Family-agnostic sanity control (0.870); shows the gain is not just calibrating the overall scale.\"},\n{\"name\":\"Label-shuffled control\",\"role\":\"ablation\",\"include_reason\":\"Negative control (1.423) showing the ridge fit uses the statistic-to-target relation rather than fitting artefacts. Describe only as the evaluator's shuffled-label control; do not invent finer feature ablations.\"},\n{\"name\":\"Relabeling-invariance check\",\"role\":\"supporting\",\"include_reason\":\"perm_max_rel_dev=0.0 documents that predictions depend only on relabeling-invariant statistics (validity check, not a performance claim).\"}],\n\"results_focus\":[\n\"Single direct comparison of family-macro log MAE (sealed final): ridge 0.181 vs constant 0.870, shuffled 1.423, 2m(n-1) bound 1.754; improvement_vs_bound 1.572 (consistent with 1.754-0.181).\",\n\"Monte Carlo uncertainty: median relative SE of labels ~0.029 (log-scale ~0.03 order), much smaller than the 0.181 model error, so label noise is a minor part of the measured error; present as a noise-floor context, not as a confidence interval on the model score.\",\n\"Episode variability: 3 seeded episodes (201-203) all gave identical score -0.18137 (deterministic candidate, fixed test graphs/labels) so episode-to-episode spread is zero and must NOT be presented as sampling uncertainty over graphs; state that uncertainty over graph draws was not measured.\",\n\"Qualification: outcome qualified, status completed, correct=true (final.qualification.*); candidate_diagnostics_trust is 'unverified' - disclose. No failed gates to discuss; do not claim validity beyond the reported qualification.\",\n\"Scope and unknowns: per-family errors, per-size errors, and which families the predictor fails on are NOT available; write as an explicit open item. Describe the test set composition (12 families, 2 test graphs each, 24 total; 36 final train graphs, 3 per family) only if drawn from the task evaluator/resources and phrase as design description.\",\n\"Search vs final separation: search baseline score -0.1913 (delta 0.0, 0 of 1 attempts scored) is a different evaluation scope from final -0.1814; do not compare them as an improvement. Unscored attempt = missing evidence.\"],\n\"figure_plan\":[\n\"Fig 1 (overview, early, page 1-2): concept schematic of the pipeline - graph from a family -> five cheap statistics -> ridge on log cover time -> prediction compared to Monte Carlo label, against the 2m(n-1) bound, with the family-macro log-error aggregation hierarchy.\",\n\"Fig 2 (main result): bar chart of family-macro log MAE for the four predictors (ridge, constant, shuffled, 2m(n-1) bound) with annotation of the Monte Carlo median relative SE as context; no error bars unless grounded (none are).\"],\n\"figure_specs\":[\n{\"figure_id\":\"overview_pipeline\",\"required\":True,\"purpose\":\"Glance-value summary of the studied object: statistics-only predictor vs worst-case bound, MC ground truth, and evaluation aggregation (graph -> family mean -> family macro mean -> episode mean).\",\"figure_type\":\"diagram\",\"preferred_generator\":\"generate-concept-figure\",\"group_by\":\"pipeline_stage\",\"metric\":\"none\",\"split_by\":\"none\",\"preferred_span\":\"full_width\",\"target_width_fraction\":1.0,\"layout_rationale\":\"ICLR template is single-column (~5.5in text width); a left-to-right 4-5 box pipeline with readable labels needs the full text width; place on page 1-2.\",\"allow_progression\":False,\"max_panels\":1,\"max_categories_per_panel\":6,\"max_series_per_panel\":2},\n{\"figure_id\":\"main_comparison\",\"required\":True,\"purpose\":\"Compare family-macro log MAE of ridge predictor against 2m(n-1) bound, constant, and shuffled controls on the sealed final test graphs.\",\"figure_type\":\"bar\",\"preferred_generator\":\"matplotlib\",\"group_by\":\"method\",\"metric\":\"macro_log_mae (lower is better)\",\"split_by\":\"none\",\"preferred_span\":\"full_width\",\"target_width_fraction\":0.7,\"layout_rationale\":\"Only 4 bars in one panel; at 0.7 of the single-column text width, tick labels and value annotations stay >=8pt without shrinking. Export PDF + 300 DPI PNG from source; reference the PDF in LaTeX.\",\"allow_progression\":False,\"max_panels\":1,\"max_categories_per_panel\":4,\"max_series_per_panel\":1}],\n\"supplementary_plan\":{\n\"purpose\":\"Give reproducibility and protocol depth that does not fit the body: exact predictor definition, evaluation metric hierarchy, qualification/diagnostic details, and search-vs-final scope separation. Nothing essential to the central claim is hidden here.\",\n\"planned_subsections\":[\n{\"heading\":\"Predictor specification and hyperparameters\",\"grounded_content\":\"Feature definitions, standardisation, ridge strength 1.0, unpenalised intercept, bound fallback, relabeling-invariance requirement, as in the frozen program source.\",\"source_ids\":[\"study.selection_kind\",\"study.search_score\"]},\n{\"heading\":\"Evaluation protocol and metric definitions\",\"grounded_content\":\"Per-graph clipped log error min(|ln(pred/MC)|,10), family mean, family-macro mean, mean over episodes with seeds 201-203; definitions of constant, shuffled, bound controls, improvement_vs_bound, perm_max_rel_dev, mc_rel_se_median; table of all final metrics.\",\"source_ids\":[\"final.metric.macro_log_mae\",\"final.metric.bound_macro_log_mae\",\"final.metric.const_macro_log_mae\",\"final.metric.shuffle_macro_log_mae\",\"final.metric.improvement_vs_bound\",\"final.metric.perm_max_rel_dev\",\"final.metric.mc_rel_se_median\"]},\n{\"heading\":\"Episode records and qualification status\",\"grounded_content\":\"Table of the three episodes (seed, score, duration), qualification fields, and the 'unverified' candidate-diagnostics trust note.\",\"source_ids\":[\"final.evidence.episodes\",\"final.qualification.outcome\",\"final.qualification.status\",\"final.qualification.correct\"]},\n{\"heading\":\"Search-stage context\",\"grounded_content\":\"Frozen-selection provenance: investigation completed with no winner, 1 attempt unscored, search score delta 0.0, baseline search score; clearly marked as a different evaluation scope from the sealed final.\",\"source_ids\":[\"study.investigation_outcome\",\"study.attempts.total\",\"study.attempts.scored\",\"study.attempts.unscored\",\"study.search_score_delta\",\"study.baseline_score\"]},\