t that the final candidate-diagnostics trust is 'unverified' and that qualification (qualified/completed) is an evaluator outcome, not a proof of validity beyond it.\",\n\"Body budget 8-9 ICLR pages with thin evidence: spend space on (a) precise problem framing and why 2m(n-1)=sum-over-edges bound is loose on small graphs, (b) full method specification enabling reimplementation, (c) metric/aggregation design and why clipped log error is used, (d) a careful threats-to-validity and limitations section (small test set, family confound, deterministic episodes, distribution shift of sizes, labels are MC estimates), (e) related work on Aleliunas et al., Feige, Lovasz. No padding; if the evidence cannot honestly fill 8 pages, prefer substantive discussion over invented experiments.\",\n\"Cite only entries in references.bib (Feige upper/lower bound entries present; verify others before citing). Starter literature (Aleliunas et al., Lovasz survey) must be cited only if present in references.bib.\",\n\"Figure export: PDF and 300 DPI PNG from source; reference the PDF in LaTeX; if raster-only, >=2400 px for full width; never upscale. Only one figure uses generate-concept-figure (overview).\",\n\"Visible metric name: 'family-macro log MAE' (lower is better). Use 'seeded run' / 'model variant' terminology per the presentation contract. Double-blind: no author or repo links; include LLM Usage section (may be in appendix).\"],\n\"failure_reason\":\"\"}\njson.dump(d,open('paper_strategy.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nE\npython3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('paper_strategy.json'))\" && grep -E \"^@\" references.bib; ls global_memory; tail -3 global_memory/memory.jsonl"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2527,"cache_read_input_tokens":43797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2527,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"servi